WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.133
-Welcome, welcome, welcome,

00:00:02.133 --> 00:00:03.601
welcome to "the Tonight Show,"
everybody.

00:00:03.601 --> 00:00:05.133
Thank you for being here.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.133 --> 00:00:07.801
Today is Monday.
-Wow.

00:00:07.801 --> 00:00:12.200
-Happy Monday.
Today is Cyber Monday.

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:14.601
Yeah.
I love shopping on Cyber Monday,

00:00:14.601 --> 00:00:16.701
'cause nothing beats spending
the holiday season

00:00:16.701 --> 00:00:19.067
on hold with the Bank of America
fraud department.

00:00:19.067 --> 00:00:20.734
[ Laughter ]
"Huh?

00:00:20.734 --> 00:00:23.667
No, I didn't buy a TV from
Walmart in the Philippines.

00:00:23.667 --> 00:00:26.400
No, that wasn't me."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:29.234
Yep, over 60 million people
bought gifts today,

00:00:29.234 --> 00:00:31.868
yet somehow, on Christmas, all
we do is exchange gift cards.

00:00:31.868 --> 00:00:35.567
How does that work?
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:00:35.567 --> 00:00:38.234
But it was a big day.
Amazon offered tons of deals,

00:00:38.234 --> 00:00:40.267
Target rolled out
major discounts,

00:00:40.267 --> 00:00:42.868
and RadioShack was like, "We
should really get a website."

00:00:42.868 --> 00:00:44.334
[ Laughter ]
"We should do that.

00:00:44.334 --> 00:00:46.601
Maybe next year.
Make a note."

00:00:46.601 --> 00:00:48.467
Yep, most people
prefer online shopping

00:00:48.467 --> 00:00:50.734
because it's easier
and because we're tired of

00:00:50.734 --> 00:00:53.834
having to sadly raise our hand
at the self-checkout machines.

00:00:53.834 --> 00:00:55.200
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:57.400
"I'm an adult who needs help.
Thanks."

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:59.367
[ Laughter ]
"Do I weigh my bag,

00:00:59.367 --> 00:01:01.634
or give me the bag, and --

00:01:01.634 --> 00:01:03.167
Just give me --
I'll buy two bags.

00:01:03.167 --> 00:01:05.300
What is --"
[ Applause ]

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:07.767
"How did it know that I didn't
put the thing in the bag."

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:09.501
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.501 --> 00:01:12.534
What's going on?
Meanwhile, today, in Washington,

00:01:12.534 --> 00:01:14.501
First Lady Jill Biden revealed
this year's

00:01:14.501 --> 00:01:16.467
White House holiday decorations.

00:01:16.467 --> 00:01:21.434
There are 41 Christmas trees
and almost 80,000 lights.

00:01:21.434 --> 00:01:24.434
Meanwhile, the family
at 1602 Pennsylvania Avenue

00:01:24.434 --> 00:01:27.334
is like, "They always
have to one-up us every year.

00:01:27.334 --> 00:01:28.834
They gotta one-up."

00:01:28.834 --> 00:01:30.501
The theme
of this year's decorations

00:01:30.501 --> 00:01:33.400
is Gifts from the Heart.

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:34.601
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:01:34.601 --> 00:01:36.267
As opposed to today's theme,

00:01:36.267 --> 00:01:38.567
Gifts I Found Online
for 60% Off.

00:01:38.567 --> 00:01:39.801
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.801 --> 00:01:41.167
Kinda from the heart, yeah.

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:43.634
Yet there are 41 Christmas trees
in the White House,

00:01:43.634 --> 00:01:45.534
and even former President Trump

00:01:45.534 --> 00:01:46.968
made it onto
one of the ornaments.

00:01:46.968 --> 00:01:48.701
This is real.
This is a real ornament.

00:01:48.701 --> 00:01:50.234
Take a look at this.

00:01:50.234 --> 00:01:51.367
You see him?
There he is.

00:01:51.367 --> 00:01:53.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:55.200
You know that's definitely
on the side of the tree

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:59.434
that faces the wall, you know?
[ Laughter ]

00:01:59.434 --> 00:02:02.067
"You made that yourself?
Let me hang it up."

00:02:02.067 --> 00:02:04.200
[ Applause ]

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:06.100
Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah,
amazing, amazing.

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:07.534
It looks like a reindeer.

00:02:07.534 --> 00:02:09.534
It looks just like you made a
reindeer out of pop sticks.

00:02:09.534 --> 00:02:12.234
There you go, back there.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.234 --> 00:02:13.667
'Course, the big news
that everyone is talking about

00:02:13.667 --> 00:02:17.334
is this new COVID variant,
called omicron.

00:02:17.334 --> 00:02:19.100
Yeah, we need another variant

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:21.000
like we another
turkey sandwich for lunch.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.167
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.167 --> 00:02:23.467
Omicron.

00:02:23.467 --> 00:02:25.767
It sounds like a Transformer
who can't smell or taste.

00:02:25.767 --> 00:02:28.801
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.801 --> 00:02:33.467
"Omicron!"
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:33.467 --> 00:02:36.767
We're getting kind of deep
in the Greek alphabet, you know?

00:02:36.767 --> 00:02:38.200
Pretty soon, we're gonna
run out of letters

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:41.000
and just start using Gatorade
flavors, you know?

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:43.267
Fauci will be like,
"We have to do whatever it takes

00:02:43.267 --> 00:02:45.601
to stop
the fierce melon variant."

00:02:45.601 --> 00:02:48.534
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.534 --> 00:02:50.033
Yeah, basically,
everyone is bummed out

00:02:50.033 --> 00:02:51.200
about the new variant.

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:53.934
Meanwhile, Delta Airlines
is like, "Oh, yeah!

00:02:53.934 --> 00:02:56.033
Hey-ya!
What's up?!

00:02:56.033 --> 00:02:57.667
I knew we were gonna --
Come on!"

00:02:57.667 --> 00:02:59.801
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.801 --> 00:03:02.267
But the White House
is trying to handle it today.

00:03:02.267 --> 00:03:04.234
President Biden
held a press conference,

00:03:04.234 --> 00:03:05.968
and he told Americans
that the new variant

00:03:05.968 --> 00:03:09.701
is a cause for concern,
not a cause for panic.

00:03:09.701 --> 00:03:11.734
Americans heard and were like,
"Well, in that case,

00:03:11.734 --> 00:03:14.234
we'll just buy 10 pallets of
toilet paper instead of 12."

00:03:14.234 --> 00:03:16.534
[ Laughter ]

00:03:16.534 --> 00:03:18.234
But the White House said
it will take two weeks

00:03:18.234 --> 00:03:20.834
to have definitive data
on the new strain.

00:03:20.834 --> 00:03:23.734
That's right, even our COVID
information has shipping delays.

00:03:23.734 --> 00:03:26.167
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.167 --> 00:03:28.567
Unbelievable.

00:03:28.567 --> 00:03:33.167
[ Applause ]
Of course -- [ Chuckles ]

00:03:33.167 --> 00:03:35.834
Of course, Biden told everyone
to get their booster.

00:03:35.834 --> 00:03:37.300
And he said
to carve out some time,

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:40.367
because rolling up your sleeves
takes longer than you think.

00:03:47.067 --> 00:03:50.100
-Is the First Lady getting one,
as well, Mr. President?

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:53.267
-She's gonna get one.
I think she's teaching.

00:03:53.267 --> 00:03:55.734
But she's gonna get one, yes.

00:03:55.734 --> 00:03:57.467
-Mr. President
what do you say...

00:03:57.467 --> 00:04:02.334
-What in the world?!
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.334 --> 00:04:03.834
Oh, my God.

00:04:03.834 --> 00:04:06.534
[ Laughter ]

00:04:06.534 --> 00:04:08.167
Oh, my gosh.
At that point,

00:04:08.167 --> 00:04:10.734
Just take your shirt off.
What are we --

00:04:10.734 --> 00:04:13.033
What is going on?
[ Applause ]

00:04:13.033 --> 00:04:15.667
[ Laughter ]

00:04:15.667 --> 00:04:17.667
Never seen anything like it.

00:04:17.667 --> 00:04:19.167
Some major business news.

00:04:19.167 --> 00:04:23.167
Today, Jack Dorsey stepped down
as the CEO of Twitter.

00:04:23.167 --> 00:04:25.000
[ Scattered cheers ]
Yep.

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:26.701
Twitter hopes
that his replacement can find

00:04:26.701 --> 00:04:28.767
new and exciting ways
for strangers

00:04:28.767 --> 00:04:30.234
to say horrible things
to each other.

00:04:30.234 --> 00:04:31.934
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.934 --> 00:04:33.667
I think Dorsey
made the right decision, though.

00:04:33.667 --> 00:04:35.434
It seems like the job
really took a toll on him.

00:04:35.434 --> 00:04:38.734
Here he is nine years ago.
That's him.

00:04:38.734 --> 00:04:40.801
And here he is today.
This is real.

00:04:40.801 --> 00:04:44.133
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.133 --> 00:04:46.801
Even Obama's like,
"Man, that job really aged you."

00:04:46.801 --> 00:04:50.501
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:50.501 --> 00:04:54.033
That's real.
I mean...

00:04:54.033 --> 00:04:57.434
It's definitely a sign to leave
your job when you're 45

00:04:57.434 --> 00:04:59.534
and you look like Tom Hanks
at the end of "Castaway."

00:04:59.534 --> 00:05:02.100
You know what I'm saying?
[ Laughter ]

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:04.801
Some news from overseas.
Apparently, Kim Jong-un

00:05:04.801 --> 00:05:07.868
banned leather coats
in North Korea

00:05:07.868 --> 00:05:10.200
so that nobody
can copy his style.

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:11.701
[ Laughter ]
This is real.

00:05:11.701 --> 00:05:13.968
Can we see him
in his leather jacket?

00:05:13.968 --> 00:05:15.667
-Yeah.
[ Audience groans ]

00:05:15.667 --> 00:05:18.033
Right now, there's a giant
police raid in the sofa section

00:05:18.033 --> 00:05:19.200
at Raymour &amp; Flanigan.

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:21.133
[ Laughter ]

00:05:21.133 --> 00:05:23.367
Well, get this -- due to
a huge snowstorm in the U.K.,

00:05:23.367 --> 00:05:27.033
more than 60 people, including
members of an Oasis cover band,

00:05:27.033 --> 00:05:30.133
have been stuck in a pub
since Friday night.

00:05:30.133 --> 00:05:31.200
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:32.601
Yeah.
After three days,

00:05:32.601 --> 00:05:34.167
everyone was fighting
with each other.

00:05:34.167 --> 00:05:36.400
It was almost like
they were in the band Oasis.

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:38.033
[ Laughter ]

00:05:38.033 --> 00:05:40.400
Almost.

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:41.767
And finally,
this is going viral.

00:05:41.767 --> 00:05:44.234
Someone filmed a fellow driver
on the highway

00:05:44.234 --> 00:05:46.100
with a Christmas tree
that might have been

00:05:46.100 --> 00:05:47.601
just a bit too big
for their car.

00:05:47.601 --> 00:05:48.701
Take a look at this.

00:05:48.701 --> 00:05:49.868
♪♪

00:05:49.868 --> 00:05:52.501
[ Laughter ]

00:05:52.501 --> 00:05:57.734
♪♪

00:05:57.734 --> 00:05:59.501
-He was like,
"This is gonna look great

00:05:59.501 --> 00:06:00.801
in my studio apartment."

